      "pins": ["FCC1.11", "FCC1.27", "FCC1.50", "FCC1.75", "FCC1.100", "NAVC1.19", "NAVC1.32", "NAVC1.48", "NAVC1.64", "NAVC1.18", "NAVC1.63", "NAVC1.12"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)", "unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad27)", "unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad50)", "unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad75)", "unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad100)", "unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)", "unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad32)", "unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad48)", "unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad64)", "Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18)", "unconnected-(NAVC1-VSSA-Pad12)", "+3V3", "+3.3V", "GND"],
      "observed": "All VDD pins of both MCUs are on unconnected nets. NAVC1.18 and NAVC1.63 are together on an isolated net rather than GND, and NAVC1.12 (VSSA) is unconnected. The +3V3 net contains MCU bypass capacitors but no MCU VDD pins; it is also distinct from the +3.3V net driven by REG2.",
      "expected": "Both MCUs' VDD pins should connect to the regulated 3.3 V rail, and their VSS/VSSA pins should connect to ground. The specification says the 3.3 V rail feeds both MCUs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"11\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\") (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"19\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18)\") (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"18\")) (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"63\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3V feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCUs have no connected supply on their VDD pins, and the NAVC also lacks a ground return for its VSS pins and a ground reference for VSSA. The flight computers therefore cannot operate as intended.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["FCC1", "NAVC1", "HSE1", "HSE2", "C32", "C33", "C52", "C53"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.5", "FCC1.37", "FCC1.12", "FCC1.13", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "Net-(C33-Pad1)", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC", "Net-(C53-Pad1)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH1)"],
      "observed": "The FCC crystal nets connect to FCC1.5 (PE6) and FCC1.37 (PE7), not its PH0/PH1 oscillator pins. For NAVC, the crystal nets have no MCU pin nodes; NAVC1.5 (PH0) and NAVC1.6 (PH1) instead connect to C37/C38 nets that go to ground.",
      "expected": "Each MCU's HSE crystal should connect between its oscillator input and output pins. The netlist identifies FCC1.12/13 as PH0/PH1, and NAVC1.5/6 as PH0/PH1.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\")) (node (ref \"HSE1\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\")) (node (ref \"R23\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") (node (ref \"C52\") (pin \"1\")) (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(NAVC1-PH0)\") (node (ref \"C37\") (pin \"1\")) (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PH0\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU has a correctly connected HSE crystal. The FCC crystal is routed to non-oscillator GPIOs, while the NAVC crystal is disconnected from the MCU oscillator pins, preventing the intended external clock operation.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["U2"],
      "pins": ["U2.1", "U2.2", "U2.3", "U2.4", "U2.5", "U2.24"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "GND"],
      "observed": "PCA9685 pin A0 (U2.1) is tied to +3.3V, while A1–A4 and A5 (U2.2–5 and U2.24) are tied to GND, selecting address 0x41.",
      "expected": "The specification gives the PCA9685 I2C address as 0x40, which requires all address pins low.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+3.3V\") (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"A0\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"GND\") (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"3\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"4\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"5\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"24\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Firmware or equipment expecting the PCA9685 at 0x40 will not communicate with it at its selected address 0x41.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: the MCU supply and ground connections are open, the HSE crystal paths are incorrectly connected, and the PCA9685 address pins select 0x41 rather than the specified 0x40. These connectivity issues prevent the board from behaving as intended."
}

